<BaseLayout title="UK council tax coverage" description="What UK Council Tax covers in England, Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland, and why their figures differ." path="/coverage/">
<header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Four nations, distinct systems</p><h1>What the figures cover</h1><p class="lede">A useful comparison starts with knowing what is included.</p></header>
<div class="task-nav section">
<a class="card" href="/councils/"><strong>England: 296 billing authorities</strong><span>Bands A to H, 2024/25 to 2026/27. Whole area charges include average parish precepts. National Band D component breakdowns and parish returns. Long-term Band D series from 1993/94 where available.</span></a>
<a class="card" href="/scotland/"><strong>Scotland: 32 councils</strong><span>Bands A to H, 2024/25 to 2026/27. Council tax only, excluding water and sewerage charges.</span></a>
<a class="card" href="/wales/"><strong>Wales: 22 councils</strong><span>2026/27 Band D averages and county, community and police components. Whole pounds as displayed in the source. Other bands are not yet included.</span></a>
<a class="card" href="https://www.nidirect.gov.uk/articles/how-rate-bills-are-calculated"><strong>Northern Ireland: domestic rates</strong><span>A different system, based on capital value and regional and district rates. Use the official guide to calculate a rate bill.</span></a>
</div>
<div class="prose"><h2>Why there is no UK league table</h2><p>England's area averages, Scotland's council-only charges and Wales's rounded Band D averages are different measures. Combining them into one ranking would obscure those differences. The comparison tool currently compares English councils of the same type and year.</p><h2>What we do not yet hold</h2><p>Property-level bands, all-band parish charges nationwide, Welsh community-level precepts, exact address-level bills, household eligibility decisions and Northern Ireland rate schedules are not included. England has 10,245 records from the national parish return, including four ceased entries, and Band D component breakdowns for all 296 billing authorities. The <a href="/precepts/">Burnley local schedule</a> covers eight parishes and the unparished area. A published area average is a reference point; your council's bill is the amount payable.</p><h2>Sources</h2><p><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/council-tax-levels-set-by-local-authorities-in-england-2026-to-2027">MHCLG England tables</a> · <a href="https://www.gov.scot/publications/council-tax-datasets/">Scottish Government band tables</a> · <a href="https://www.gov.wales/council-tax-levels-april-2026-march-2027">Welsh Government 2026/27 tables</a>. Sources reviewed 5 October 2026.</p></div>
</BaseLayout>
